alert tls $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:"Possible exfiltration to personal NAS over Tailscale mesh-VPN tunnel (tailnet)"; flow:to_server,established; tls.sni; content:".ts.net"; nocase; endswith; fast_pattern; threshold:type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 3600; metadata: author Arnold Chan, mitre_technique_id T1572, mitre_technique_id T1567; classtype:policy-violation; sid:1000201; rev:2;)
# POLICY/HUNT RULE - Tailscale traffic is not inherently malicious; this SNI-based match cannot distinguish sanctioned corporate tailnets from personal/unauthorized ones. Environment-specific tuning REQUIRED: define $SANCTIONED_TAILNET with your organization's known/approved Tailscale exit-node or coordination-server IP ranges and add "!$SANCTIONED_TAILNET" as a destination exclusion once populated.

alert udp $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET 41641 (msg:"Tailscale WireGuard mesh-VPN handshake to external host (possible tailnet exfil channel)"; flow:to_server; dsize:>0; threshold:type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 3600; metadata: author detections.ai, mitre_technique_id T1572, mitre_technique_id T1567; classtype:policy-violation; sid:1000202; rev:2;)
# POLICY/HUNT RULE - WireGuard handshakes on UDP/41641 are generated by every legitimate Tailscale client, not just illicit exfil tunnels; network telemetry alone cannot separate sanctioned corporate mesh-VPN use from personal/unauthorized tailnets. Environment-specific tuning REQUIRED: define $SANCTIONED_TAILNET with your organization's known/approved Tailscale exit-node or coordination-server IP ranges and add "!$SANCTIONED_TAILNET" as a destination exclusion once populated.